{
 "after_section": 1,
 "caption": "A non-blocking write of 70000 bytes copies only what fits, 65536, and returns 65536 while 4464 bytes stay in user space. The reader takes 8192, freeing exactly enough for the second write of 4464, so the pipe ends holding 61808 bytes.",
 "spec": {
  "type": "blocks",
  "direction": "down",
  "title": "Worked example: capacity 65536 B, then read 8192 B, then write 4464 B",
